course: dictionary
lesson: 11906
title: Bungee: a stretchy word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A bungee is a long, stretchy rope or cord. When you read «Mum used a bungee to hold the bags on the roof», the clues are bags and roof. A bungee holds things in place, so it must be a stretchy strap.
explain: Context also helps with bungee jumping. «Sam tied a bungee to his ankles and jumped from the high bridge.» A cord tied to your ankles and a jump from a high place tell you the sport is exciting, and the cord makes you bounce up and down.
explain: Check a meaning by swapping it into the sentence. In «Dad bungeed the tent onto the car roof», the verb bungeed means fastened with stretchy straps. If that still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: A bungee is a long, stretchy rope or cord.
fact: «Bungee jumping» means jumping from a high place with a cord tied to your ankles.
fact: A bungee cord is an elastic strap with hooks, used to hold luggage on a bike rack or roof rack.
fact: New Zealand is famous for bungee jumping from bridges.
fact: In science, a stretched bungee stores elastic energy and pulls back as it springs.
exercise: «Mum used a bungee to hold the bags on the roof rack.» What is a bungee here? | A tall tower | A kind of small boat | *A stretchy strap with hooks | A type of bird
exercise: «Sam tied a bungee to his ankles and jumped from the bridge.» What is bungee jumping? | Climbing a tree with a rope | *Jumping from a high place with a stretchy cord tied to your ankles | Walking slowly across a bridge | Swimming in a deep lake
exercise: «Dad bungeed the tent onto the car roof.» What does bungeed mean here? | *Fastened with stretchy straps | Painted in bright colours | Folded up small | Dropped on the ground
test: «When a stretched bungee pulls you back up, it uses stored energy.» What is stored in a stretched bungee? | *Elastic energy | Heat from the sun | Water | Sound
test: «Ella bungeed her bag onto the bike rack.» Which word is the verb in this sentence? | Ella | *bungeed | rack | bike
exam: Tom says, «Let's bungee the tent to the car.» What does bungee mean here? | *To fasten with stretchy cords | To swim fast | To dig a hole | To sing loudly
